    <div class="content-box step-card">
        <span class="step-pill">Step 3</span>
        <h2 class="content-title"><i class="fa-solid fa-magnifying-glass"></i> Complete the Missions</h2>
        <p>Follow the instructions in the <strong>Messages</strong> app. Here’s what to look for:</p>

        <ul class="custom-list">
            <li><strong>Browser:</strong> Look at the Cookie Banner. What is the difference between “Necessary” and “All” cookies?</li>
            <li><strong>Connectify:</strong> Read the permissions carefully. Does a social app really need your location <em>all the time</em>? Check the Terms & Conditions for the “Data Retention” rule.</li>
            <li><strong>MapMe:</strong> Compare “While Using App” vs “Always Allow”. Why would an app want to track you when you aren't using it?</li>
            <li><strong>SkyWatch:</strong> Try “Approximate Location”. Do you still get the weather? What is the privacy benefit?</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="grid-2-col">
        <div class="content-box step-card">
            <span class="step-pill">Step 4</span>
            <h2 class="content-title"><i class="fa-solid fa-pen-to-square"></i> Reflection</h2>

            <div class="callout">
                <h3 style="font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--primary-color); margin: 0;"><strong>A.</strong> The “greediest” app</h3>
                <p>Which app asked for the most data? Did it seem justified?</p>
            </div>

            <div class="callout">
                <h3 style="font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--primary-color); margin: 0;"><strong>B.</strong> The trade-off</h3>
                <p>Give one example where you chose between <strong>privacy</strong> (keeping data safe) and <strong>convenience</strong> (making the app easier to use). What did you choose and why?</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="content-box step-card">
            <span class="step-pill">Step 5</span>
            <h2 class="content-title"><i class="fa-solid fa-comments"></i> Partner Discussion</h2>
            <p>Compare your “Data Footprint” score with your partner. Who has more items in their footprint? Why?</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="callout">
        <h2 class="content-title"><i class="fa-solid fa-graduation-cap"></i> By the end of this task, you should be able to…</h2>
        <ul class="custom-list" style="margin-bottom: 0;">
            <li>Identify common permissions apps ask for (location, photos, tracking)</li>
            <li>Explain the trade-offs between privacy and functionality</li>
            <li>Understand that “free” apps often pay for themselves with your data</li>
            <li>Make informed choices about app permissions</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
